# Trivy ignore list.
#
# Every entry here is a proven, individually-investigated exception, not a way to make
# scan output quiet. Enforcement is severity: HIGH,CRITICAL with exit-code: 1 in
# .github/workflows/ci.yml — a real HIGH or CRITICAL finding in anything this ignores
# would still need its own separate entry, and would not silently pass because the
# module happens to appear here for an unrelated reason.

# GO-2026-5932 — golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp: unmaintained, unsafe by design, no fix
# available (Trivy reports "Fixed Version: " empty; govulncheck confirms "Fixed in: N/A").
# Pulled in transitively as a required module, not imported or called anywhere in NEXUS's
# own code — `govulncheck ./...` reports "0 vulnerabilities" in the symbol-reachability
# scan and lists this only under modules required but never called. Its own advisory
# severity is UNKNOWN rather than HIGH or CRITICAL; it reached CI's HIGH,CRITICAL
# enforcement gate only because of how the pinned Trivy CLI version (bundled inside
# aquasecurity/trivy-action) classifies Go vulnerability database advisories that carry
# no CVSS rating. There is nothing to remediate: no fixed version exists to upgrade to,
# and the code path is not reachable. Re-verify with `govulncheck ./...` after any
# golang.org/x/crypto bump, since a genuinely fixed release would make this line stale.
GO-2026-5932
